      "math_academy_id": "q-164233",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}=-1$, find its $z$-intercepts.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $z$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}-{z}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ -{z}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =1 \\\\ z & =\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $z=-1$ and $z=1.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-1)$ and $(0,0,1).$",
